{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A column is any set of vertices: empty columns and repeated columns are kept, and a graph’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop is the one bit at its vertex, the hyperedge {v}. (NetworkX’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidence_matrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"loop a zero column; Godsil–Royle’s entry 2 is not a bit. A zero column would forget the loop.)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the directed form; ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the sparse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representation of the same hypergraphs.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Storage.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Both orientations are stored, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" stores its rows: n rows of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"⌈m\/64⌉ words and m columns of ⌈n\/64⌉ words, with the row and column popcounts cached. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"members(ofHyperedgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are each one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BitSet"},{"type":"text","text":" copy of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"⌈n\/64⌉ or ⌈m\/64⌉ words, a cell edit writes two bits in O(1), and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transposed()"},{"type":"text","text":", the dual,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"swaps the two in O(1). The cost is 2·n·m\/8 bytes: "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the matrix is for dense or small"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidence"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (spectral work at n·m up to about 10⁹, hypergraphs with large hyperedges). Sparse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidence belongs in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Equality compares cell for cell, with equal shape: column order is observable, because a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"column’s position is what a spectral caller indexes by. (","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s equality","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ignores positions; convert to compare that way.)","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init()","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-4158r","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-4kjv4","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-4zxvg","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-5i569","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-91168","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-mnxt","doc:\/